>> title: Karaage
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: chicken, japanese, deep-fry, potato starch, appetiser
>> counters: Ramen Shop, The Bowl Shop, Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: karaage, kara-age, から揚げ, 唐揚げ, tori karaage, torikara, Japanese fried chicken, fried chicken pieces, chicken karaage
>> pairs-with: shoyu-ramen, gyoza
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — the first fry cooks it through and the second crisps it; a single fry gives you one or the other and never both

>> step: Two fries, not one.
Two fries, not one.

>> step: marinate 30 min
Marinate @boneless chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; skin on, cut into 2-in pieces) in @soy sauce{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @sake{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @mirin{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated), @garlic{2%cloves}(grated), @granulated sugar{1%tsp}(4 g) and @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}(5 mL) ~marinate{30%min} at room temperature.

>> step: beat the egg through
Beat @egg{1%large}(50 g) through @&(~1)marinated chicken{} until every piece is slick with it.

>> step: dredge, then let it hydrate 5 min
Dredge @&(~1)chicken{} piece by piece in @potato starch{3/4%cup}(110 g), pressing it on, then ~rest{5%min} on a rack.

>> step: fry at 320°F (160°C) 90 sec, rest 5 min
Fry @&(~1)coated chicken{} in @neutral oil{6%cups}(1.4 L; at 320°F/160°C) in batches ~fry{90%sec}, then lift it onto a rack and ~rest{5%min}.

>> step: fry again at 360°F (180°C) 60 sec
Fry @&(~1)rested chicken{} a second time at 360°F (180°C) ~fry{60%sec}, until the crust is deep gold and audibly crisp, then drain it and serve with @lemon{1}(cut in wedges) and a heavy grind of pepper.
